# 8. WORKSTREAM E — RELIABILITY AND RECOVERY

A Worker that functions only when everything is perfect is not complete.

Test at least the following failure modes.

## Process and machine failures

- Controller crashes before dispatch.
- Controller crashes during dispatch.
- Controller crashes after send but before receipt.
- Browser closes.
- Browser restarts.
- Extension service worker is suspended.
- Native host disconnects.
- Unix socket disappears.
- Host process is restarted.
- Journal write is interrupted.
- Journal data becomes malformed.
- Filesystem permissions are unsafe.

## GitHub failures

- Assignment changes mid-execution.
- PR is closed or merged.
- Head SHA changes.
- Assignment is removed.
- Duplicate webhook is received.
- Webhooks arrive out of order.
- GitHub returns incomplete or stale data.
- GitHub API is unavailable.
- CAS operation conflicts.
- Write success is uncertain.
- Ledger record cannot be read back.

## ChatGPT/browser failures

- Login expired.
- Composer missing.
- ChatGPT busy.
- Wrong tab targeted.
- Multiple matching tabs.
- Navigation during send.
- Conversation ID changed.
- Network stalls after click.
- First turn may have been sent but cannot be confirmed.
- Continuation may have been sent but cannot be confirmed.

**Never blindly retry an uncertain send.**

The correct behavior is to quarantine the attempt, retain durable evidence, and require an authorized reconciliation path.

